NAME
       glxinfo - report GLX and OpenGL information about the X display

SYNOPSIS
       glxinfo [-display displayname] [-B] [-v] [-t] [-s]

DESCRIPTION
       glxinfo lists the GLX extensions the display supports, the OpenGL
       renderer, version and extension strings, and the available visuals
       and framebuffer configurations.  It is the standard first check that
       an OpenGL stack works at all.  On LikeOS the expected renderer string
       names Mesa's llvmpipe: rendering is software, presented over XShm.

OPTIONS
       -display displayname
              Connect to the named X display instead of $DISPLAY.

       -B     Brief: print only the renderer/version block.

       -v     Verbose visual output.

       -t     Print visuals in tabular form.

       -s     Print a single extension name per line.

SEE ALSO
       glxgears(1), eglinfo(1)

